Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 02:49:31 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 24/34] [3.1.1] [M156] [Blink] Reset HTMLVideoElement snapshot
 cache on clearing player

Original change's description:
> [Blink] Reset HTMLVideoElement snapshot cache on clearing player
>
> HTMLVideoElement::CreateStaticBitmapImage() caches a
> VideoFrameAcceleratedSnapshotPool and CanvasSnapshotInfo across calls
> for up to 3 seconds (kTemporaryResourceDeletionDelay), reusing the
> pool's backing SharedImage in place when the new frame's
> CanvasSnapshotInfo (size, format, color space, alpha type) matches the
> cached info and the previous snapshot reference has been released. It
> then sets OriginClean on the returned StaticBitmapImage based on the
> current player's WouldTaintOrigin() state.
>
> Because OnWebMediaPlayerCleared() did not reset this cache, switching
> an HTMLVideoElement from a cross-origin (tainted) media source to a
> same-origin (origin-clean) media source with matching frame parameters
> within the 3-second window would reuse the SharedImage containing the
> previous cross-origin video frame's pixels. If drawing the new
> same-origin frame into that SharedImage fails to overwrite it (for
> example, if the new frame's backing SharedImage fails read access in
> the GPU process), CreateStaticBitmapImage() returns the untouched
> cross-origin pixels marked as origin-clean, allowing cross-origin pixel
> readback via canvas.
>
> Reset the snapshot cache (and stop cache_deleting_timer_) in
> HTMLVideoElement::OnWebMediaPlayerCleared() so that cached snapshot
> resources are never retained across WebMediaPlayer instances.
>
